    "b-50-workflows-a-game-moves-through-1": {
      "id": "b-50-workflows-a-game-moves-through-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A game moves through sync, run, and PR workflows. Each phase occupies its own "
        },
        {
          "insert": "HarnessState",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " workflow slot, may acquire the dispatch lease, and operates its own queue workers without creating a second source of game authority. HarnessState is the harness's per-game coordination record for revision, dispatch-lease holder, queued requests, and blockers."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-workflows-phase-model-2": {
      "id": "b-50-workflows-phase-model-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Phase Model"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-workflows-text-3": {
      "id": "b-50-workflows-text-3",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "text"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "HarnessState\n  -> sync workflow slot\n       -> baseline intake and staged reconciliation\n  -> run workflow slot\n       -> epoch queue and epoch workers\n  -> PR workflow slot\n       -> review queue and review agents\n\nDispatch lease\n  -> held by at most one active workflow\n  -> transferred only through a durable handoff"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-workflows-the-active-workflow-owns-4": {
      "id": "b-50-workflows-the-active-workflow-owns-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The active workflow owns dispatch decisions and the checkout surfaces assigned to its phase. A queued or observed workflow may record intent, but it cannot dispatch workers or mutate protected state until it holds the lease."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-workflows-knowledge-processing-use-5": {
      "id": "b-50-workflows-knowledge-processing-use-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Knowledge processing uses durable background jobs rather than a fourth game phase. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Execution Classes and Jobs",
          "attributes": {
            "link": "../60-knowledge/70-background-jobs"
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " defines which knowledge work is background-safe and which work waits for sync staging and publication."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
